AB  - The growing complexity of machine learning (ML) workflows, combined with the scale of continuous integration and continuous deployment (CI/CD) pipelines, has placed increasing pressure on infrastructure efficiency, cost-effectiveness, and deployment reliability. Traditional Kubernetes-based resource schedulers, while robust for stateless services, fall short when orchestrating dynamic, compute-intensive ML workloads. In this paper, we introduce MLPilot, a novel CI/CD-aware flight controller designed to intelligently auto-tune resource allocation across MLOps pipelines in Kubernetes environments. MLPilot integrates seamlessly with existing CI/CD tools and leverages a telemetry-driven deep reinforcement learning engine to dynamically adjust compute, memory, and GPU configurations across pipeline stages. Our system architecture includes a Kubernetes-native operator, real-time telemetry aggregator, and a learning-based policy optimizer that jointly minimize latency, reduce infrastructure cost, and enhance deployment stability. Through extensive experiments on real-world ML workloads—including NLP, computer vision, and tabular models—we demonstrate that MLPilot achieves up to 32% faster pipeline execution, 27% lower resource cost, and 20% higher GPU utilization compared to state-of-the-art baselines. These results highlight the importance of intelligent, learning-based orchestration in future MLOps deployments. Our current evaluation is on a single 3-node cluster and does not yet enforce formal safety constraints for multi-tenant isolation; we outline these as priorities for future work.
ER  - 

