AB  - GreenLoop is a sustainable waste management system that applies cloud computing and deep learning to provide real-time identification and reporting of waste drag. GreenLoop consists of an object detection model based on YOLOv8; through training using a dataset of waste dumpster images with pre-defined classes for plastics, batteries, and cardboard. The dataset was pre-processed and annotated in Roboflow. Once deployed the system consists of a lightweight Streamlit web application to upload images and visualize real-time detection of waste drag and its geographic location; thereby providing a simple path for civic organizations to accept tasks. It is important to note that a simple SQLite database was added on the back end to manage user submissions, organizations caused response and authenticating data. The full system was deployed on Streamlit Cloud. Streamlit Cloud allows global access, continuous deployment and no human maintenance or infrastructure cost. Therefore, leveraging cloud-based infrastructure, diverse machine learning techniques, datadriven operating systems, and a simplistic human interface Green Loop promotes elements of sustainable waste management practice and produces environmental sustainability in broader sense.
